[=#sqlrclientlimitations]
= Limitations =

The SQLRClient protocol is SQL Relay's own, so it has no notable feature gaps the way the emulated protocols do.  The one thing worth knowing about is that a newer client cannot talk to an older server (an older client still works against a newer server), so the server side of any link - including a //router// instance talking to the instances behind it - has to be upgraded first.

